.TH SAVAGE 1.SH NAMEsavage \- Savage's floating-point benchmark.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsavage\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONBill Savage's benchmark: a chain of functions -- tan of atan, exp of log,square of square root -- that should add one on every pass, run athousand times.  It prints\fBstart\fR,\fRthe final value and\fB1000 loops done\fR.\fRExactly right would be 1000; how far the printed value is from itmeasures the rounding of the floating-point arithmetic, and the timebetween the first and last lines its speed..nf    a = 9.99999999981959e+02.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fRTime it with your own OS-9's\fBtime\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOsieve, paranoia, dhrystone